{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '1,285p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker\n     2\t  \"The code linker (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md): fetches and verifies\n     3\t   code over a DaoJing content handle -- a local store, a\n     4\t   `dao.jing.dht/create-content-dht` handle, or a\n     5\t   `dao.jing.remote/content-client` over DaoStream.\n     6\t\n     7\t   `fetch` is one format-neutral admission-then-six-step function\n     8\t   (sections 4.1-4.2). A format record supplies the contract, the\n     9\t   identity mint and match, the row-local validator, the whole-value\n    10\t   validator, the three position-bearing scanners of section 4.1\n    11\t   (`:obligations-fn`, `:definitions-fn`, `:applications-fn`), and the\n    12\t   parts worklist; the four records are `ast-format`, `semantic-format`,\n    13\t   `stack-format`, and `register-format` (section 5). Storage\n    14\t   addresses (`jing/segment-key`) and VM identities (H, R) are separate\n    15\t   preimages for the de Bruijn formats and the same preimage for the\n    16\t   storage-derived ones, so step 2 checks the address and step 3 checks\n    17\t   the identity; neither subsumes the other (I5).\n    18\t\n    19\t   The handle, the index, the format record, and the receiver environment\n    20\t   are explicit arguments. There is no global loader, registry, callback,\n    21\t   or cache here, and every outcome -- success or refusal -- is a returned\n    22\t   plain data map (section 4.3).\"\n    23\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]])\n    24\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    25\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    26\t            [dao.space.query :as query]\n    27\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    28\t            [yin.vm.code :as code]\n    29\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as debruijn-code]\n    30\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-linearize :as linearize]\n    31\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as debruijn-register-code]\n    32\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile :as register-compile]\n    33\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-resolve :as resolve]\n    34\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t;; =============================================================================\n    38\t;; Refusal vocabulary (section 4.3)\n    39\t;; =============================================================================\n    40\t\n    41\t(def refusal-reasons\n    42\t  \"Every reason a linker refusal may carry.\"\n    43\t  #{:absent :address-mismatch :hash-mismatch :descriptor-defect\n    44\t    :parts-limit :contract-mismatch :use-before-definition\n    45\t    :unresolved-free :shadowed-free :pairing-mismatch})\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn refused\n    49\t  \"A qualified refusal: `{:status :refused, :reason reason}` merged with\n    50\t   the step's own evidence `data`.\"\n    51\t  ([reason] (refused reason {}))\n    52\t  ([reason data]\n    53\t   (merge data {:status :refused, :reason reason})))\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(defn refused?\n    57\t  \"True when `res` is a linker refusal.\"\n    58\t  [res]\n    59\t  (and (map? res) (= :refused (:status res))))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn ok?\n    63\t  \"True when `res` is a verified linker outcome.\"\n    64\t  [res]\n    65\t  (and (map? res) (= :ok (:status res))))\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t;; =============================================================================\n    69\t;; Free-name scanners (sections 5.1, 5.2)\n    70\t;; =============================================================================\n    71\t\n    72\t(defn- distinct-names\n    73\t  [names]\n    74\t  (vec (distinct names)))\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn stack-free-names\n    78\t  \"Every `:load-free` name in a canonical stack instruction vector, in pc\n    79\t   order of first appearance.\"\n    80\t  [instruction-vector]\n    81\t  (distinct-names\n    82\t    (keep (fn [t] (when (= :load-free (nth t 0)) (nth t 1)))\n    83\t          instruction-vector)))\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\t(defn register-free-names\n    87\t  \"Every `:load-free` name across all bodies of a register image map, in\n    88\t   pc order of first appearance. A register `:load-free` is\n    89\t   `[:load-free rd name]`.\"\n    90\t  [register-image-map]\n    91\t  (distinct-names\n    92\t    (keep (fn [t] (when (= :load-free (nth t 0)) (nth t 2)))\n    93\t          (:instructions register-image-map))))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn- all-var-names\n    97\t  \"The conservative fallback for a vector whose layout the scope walk\n    98\t   cannot read: every `:var` name, all free. Over-approximating\n    99\t   obligations is always admissible.\"\n   100\t  [v]\n   101\t  (set (keep (fn [t]\n   102\t               (when (and (vector? t)\n   103\t                          (= :var (nth t 0))\n   104\t                          (< 1 (count t)))\n   105\t                 (nth t 1)))\n   106\t             v)))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(defn- closure-spans\n   110\t  \"`[[c body r] ...]` for every `:closure` of canonical vector `v`: the\n   111\t   body of the closure at pc `c` is `[body r]`, `r` the first `:return`\n   112\t   at or after `body` (the out-of-line bodies of UCF section 7.3.2); nil\n   113\t   `r` when there is none.\"\n   114\t  [v]\n   115\t  (let [n (count v)]\n   116\t    (keep (fn [c]\n   117\t            (let [t (nth v c)]\n   118\t              (when (and (vector? t)\n   119\t                         (= :closure (nth t 0))\n   120\t                         (< 2 (count t)))\n   121\t                (let [body (nth t 2)]\n   122\t                  [c body\n   123\t                   (first (filter (fn [pc]\n   124\t                                    (let [u (nth v pc)]\n   125\t                                      (and (vector? u)\n   126\t                                           (= :return (nth u 0)))))\n   127\t                                  (range body n)))]))))\n   128\t          (range n))))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- spans-conform?\n   132\t  \"Whether `spans` is the closed, off-pc-0, pairwise-disjoint body layout\n   133\t   the scope walk reads; anything else rules every `:var` free.\"\n   134\t  [spans]\n   135\t  (let [pairs (map (fn [[_ b r]] [b r]) spans)]\n   136\t    (and (every? (fn [[b r]] (and r (pos? b))) pairs)\n   137\t         (= (count pairs) (count (distinct pairs)))\n   138\t         (every? (fn [[[b1 r1] [b2 r2]]] (or (< r1 b2) (< r2 b1)))\n   139\t                 (for [x pairs, y pairs :when (neg? (compare x y))]\n   140\t                   [x y])))))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(defn- vector-layout\n   144\t  \"The closure body spans of canonical vector `v` when they are the\n   145\t   closed, off-pc-0, pairwise-disjoint layout the scope walk reads, else\n   146\t   nil -- every scanner then degrades (section 4.1).\"\n   147\t  [v]\n   148\t  (let [spans (closure-spans v)]\n   149\t    (when (spans-conform? spans) spans)))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn- safe-layout\n   153\t  \"Like `vector-layout`, but a vector the walk cannot read at all (an\n   154\t   operand that throws) degrades too.\"\n   155\t  [v]\n   156\t  (try (vector-layout v)\n   157\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- in-body-pc?\n   161\t  \"Whether pc `p` lies in one of the closure body spans `spans`.\"\n   162\t  [spans p]\n   163\t  (boolean (some (fn [[_ b r]] (<= b p r)) spans)))\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\t(defn- conditional-ranges\n   167\t  \"The pcs a conditional target range covers in canonical vector `v`\n   168\t   (section 4.1): for every `:jump` or `:branch-false` at pc b with\n   169\t   target t, the pcs strictly between b and t, either direction -- the\n   170\t   fall-through a taken branch skips, and a backward jump's body.\"\n   171\t  [v]\n   172\t  (into #{}\n   173\t        (mapcat (fn [[b t]]\n   174\t                  (when (and (integer? t) (not= b t))\n   175\t                    (range (inc (min b t)) (max b t)))))\n   176\t        (keep (fn [pc]\n   177\t                (let [t (nth v pc)]\n   178\t                  (when (and (vector? t)\n   179\t                             (contains? #{:jump :branch-false}\n   180\t                                        (nth t 0)))\n   181\t                    [pc (nth t 1)])))\n   182\t              (range (count v)))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn- degraded-occurrences\n   186\t  \"The conservative degradation's own occurrence records (section 4.1):\n   187\t   every name retained at no position, inside a body -- a scanner that\n   188\t   cannot read positions retains every occurrence and discharges\n   189\t   nothing.\"\n   190\t  [names]\n   191\t  (vec (sort-by (comp str :name)\n   192\t                (map (fn [n] {:name n, :at nil, :in-body? true}) names))))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(defn- degraded-definitions\n   196\t  \"The conservative degradation's own definition records (section 4.1):\n   197\t   every key retained at no position, conditional -- a definition whose\n   198\t   position is unknown discharges nothing.\"\n   199\t  [names]\n   200\t  (vec (sort-by (comp str :name)\n   201\t                (map (fn [n] {:name n, :at nil, :conditional? true})\n   202\t                     names))))\n   203\t\n   204\t\n   205\t(defn semantic-free-occurrences\n   206\t  \"Every free `:var` occurrence of canonical vector `v` as a section 4.1\n   207\t   record `{:name sym :at pc :in-body? b}`, in pc order (UCF section\n   208\t   7.3.2): a `:var` at pc `p` is bound iff `p` lies in the body of a\n   209\t   `:closure` whose params hold the name, transitively through the body\n   210\t   holding that closure's own pc. Over a vector whose body spans are not\n   211\t   closed, off pc 0, and pairwise disjoint -- anything but the\n   212\t   ast-to-bytecode layout -- every `:var` name degrades to a record with\n   213\t   no position: over-approximating obligations is always admissible.\"\n   214\t  [v]\n   215\t  (try\n   216\t    (if-let [spans (vector-layout v)]\n   217\t      (let [params (into {}\n   218\t                         (keep (fn [c]\n   219\t                                 (let [t (nth v c)]\n   220\t                                   (when (and (vector? t)\n   221\t                                              (= :closure (nth t 0)))\n   222\t                                     [c (nth t 1)]))))\n   223\t                         (range (count v)))\n   224\t            owner (fn [pc]\n   225\t                    (some (fn [[c b r]] (when (<= b pc r) c)) spans))\n   226\t            bound? (fn bound?\n   227\t                     [pc sym]\n   228\t                     (when-let [c (owner pc)]\n   229\t                       (or (some #(= % sym) (get params c))\n   230\t                           (bound? c sym))))]\n   231\t        (vec (keep (fn [pc]\n   232\t                     (let [t (nth v pc)]\n   233\t                       (when (and (vector? t)\n   234\t                                  (= :var (nth t 0))\n   235\t                                  (< 1 (count t))\n   236\t                                  (not (bound? pc (nth t 1))))\n   237\t                         {:name (nth t 1), :at pc,\n   238\t                          :in-body? (in-body-pc? spans pc)})))\n   239\t                   (range (count v)))))\n   240\t      (degraded-occurrences (all-var-names v)))\n   241\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   242\t      (degraded-occurrences (all-var-names v)))))\n   243\t\n   244\t\n   245\t(defn semantic-free-names\n   246\t  \"Every `:var` name free at some pc of canonical vector `v` (UCF\n   247\t   section 7.3.2): the names of `semantic-free-occurrences`' records,\n   248\t   which carry the scope walk and the degradation.\"\n   249\t  [v]\n   250\t  (into #{} (map :name) (semantic-free-occurrences v)))\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\t(defn- step-order\n   254\t  \"The execution order of two occurrence-path steps of one row (section\n   255\t   6.1): a `:node` slot's step is its row position, a `:nodes` slot's\n   256\t   the pair `[position i]`. A bare position evaluates before the\n   257\t   operands of the `:nodes` slot that follows it.\"\n   258\t  [a b]\n   259\t  (cond\n   260\t    (and (integer? a) (integer? b)) (compare a b)\n   261\t    (integer? a) -1\n   262\t    (integer? b) 1\n   263\t    :else (let [n (min (count a) (count b))]\n   264\t            (loop [i 0]\n   265\t              (if (= i n)\n   266\t                (compare (count a) (count b))\n   267\t                (let [c (compare (nth a i) (nth b i))]\n   268\t                  (if (zero? c) (recur (inc i)) c)))))))\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\t(defn- path-order\n   272\t  \"The execution order of two occurrence paths from one root (section\n   273\t   4.1's tree order): slot order at the first step where they diverge.\"\n   274\t  [a b]\n   275\t  (let [n (min (count a) (count b))]\n   276\t    (loop [i 0]\n   277\t      (if (= i n)\n   278\t        (compare (count a) (count b))\n   279\t        (let [c (step-order (nth a i) (nth b i))]\n   280\t          (if (zero? c) (recur (inc i)) c))))))\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\t(defn- path-before?\n   284\t  \"True when occurrence path `d` executes before occurrence path `u`.\"\n   285\t  [d u]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
