{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '285,320p;404,476p;527,556p;1870,1910p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc | sed -n '160,181p;226,244p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '675,700p;1248,1266p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '155,215p;475,560p;1059,1135p'\"","aggregated_output":"   285\t  ;; :obligations-fn  value -> [{:name sym :at position :in-body? b}]\n   286\t  ;; :definitions-fn  value -> [{:name sym :at position\n   287\t  ;;                             :conditional? b}]\n   288\t  ;; :applications-fn value -> [{:at position}]\n   289\t  ;; position: a tree occurrence path [root-address path] for\n   290\t  ;;           :yin.ast/code; a pc for the vector formats\n   291\t  ```\n   292\t\n   293\t  `:conditional?` is true when any `:if` branch, jump target range, or\n   294\t  lambda body encloses the definition; `:in-body?` is true when a\n   295\t  lambda body encloses the occurrence; an `:applications-fn` record is\n   296\t  one **application site**: a position at which this image may apply a\n   297\t  closure it creates -- a direct call site, a call of an imported\n   298\t  name, or a call of a primitive that receives a function argument,\n   299\t  because the callee may apply what it is handed. Dominance between\n   300\t  two positions is decided by the linker from these fields and the\n   301\t  format's order (step 5a). For the AST record all three scanners are\n   302\t  Datalog over the rows: `yin.vm/free-names` today returns a symbol\n   303\t  set, and is extended (or wrapped by an occurrence-scoped query over\n   304\t  the same rules) to return each occurrence's path; the definitions\n   305\t  scanner is the store-key query behind `yin.vm/ast-requirements`\n   306\t  with the binding row's path and its enclosing tags; the application\n   307\t  scanner is the application-row query over the same relation. For\n   308\t  the vector formats all three are operand scans by pc (`:var`\n   309\t  against `:store-put`, `:load-free` against the `yin/def` call\n   310\t  sites, the call opcodes for applications) with conditional target\n   311\t  ranges taken from the `:jump-if` and body operands. A format whose\n   312\t  scanner returns positions as `nil` is admitted and falls under the\n   313\t  conservative degradation of step 5a: every occurrence is retained\n   314\t  as an obligation, and with no application positions no occurrence\n   315\t  inside a lambda body is discharged at all.\n   316\t\n   317\t`fetch` and `step` contain no branch on `:format`. Adding a fifth backend\n   318\tis one more record.\n   319\t\n   320\t### 4.2 The six steps\n   404\t   whole-tree rules that step 2's row-local check cannot run); for a\n   405\t   vector, over the vector; for a register image, including the\n   406\t   ascending, bounded, exact live-set rules. A validator that throws is\n   407\t   `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:validator-refused`.\n   408\t5. **Verify dependency closure.** Two halves.\n   409\t   - *5a, at the linker: obligations.* Two scans run over the verified\n   410\t     value. `:obligations-fn` yields the free-name occurrences, each\n   411\t     with its position: for a tree, the occurrence path and whether it\n   412\t     lies inside a `:lambda` body; for a vector, the pc and whether it\n   413\t     lies in a body rather than the main sequence. `:definitions-fn`\n   414\t     yields the **definition set** with positions: every constant store\n   415\t     key the image binds at module level (the section 7.7 store-key\n   416\t     query of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`: `:vm/store-put` rows,\n   417\t     `:store-put` operands, `yin/def` applications with a constant key),\n   418\t     each with the position of the binding in the main sequence.\n   419\t     A definition discharges an occurrence by **defined-before-use\n   420\t     under control-flow dominance**, not by subtraction of names and\n   421\t     not by source order alone. Source order says a definition is\n   422\t     written earlier; dominance says it has executed by the time the\n   423\t     occurrence runs. Only the second discharges, and where dominance\n   424\t     cannot be established the obligation is **retained**, never\n   425\t     dropped:\n   426\t     - A definition is *unconditional* when it sits in the main\n   427\t       sequence at top level or inside a `:do` (for a tree) or at a pc\n   428\t       in the main sequence outside every conditional target range\n   429\t       (for a vector); it is *conditional* when any `:if` branch, any\n   430\t       jump target, or any lambda body encloses it. A conditional\n   431\t       definition discharges nothing statically: the linker cannot know\n   432\t       the branch was taken, so an occurrence that depends on it keeps\n   433\t       its obligation and is checked at the receiver under 5b exactly\n   434\t       as an undefined name would be, and the manifest must declare it\n   435\t       or the link is `:undeclared-free`. This is conservative by\n   436\t       design: a module that defines a name only in one branch and\n   437\t       reads it afterwards must declare what the name means when the\n   438\t       branch is not taken.\n   439\t     - An occurrence in the main sequence (outside every lambda body)\n   440\t       is discharged only by an unconditional definition of that name\n   441\t       that dominates it: for a tree, an earlier sibling in the same\n   442\t       or an enclosing top-level `:do`; for a vector, an earlier pc in\n   443\t       the main sequence with no conditional target range between the\n   444\t       two. A main-sequence occurrence whose only definitions are all\n   445\t       later or all conditional and later is `:use-before-definition`:\n   446\t       in the isolated store it would read nothing, and no manifest\n   447\t       declaration may stand in for a name the module itself defines\n   448\t       unconditionally later. An occurrence whose only definitions are\n   449\t       conditional and earlier retains its obligation, per the rule\n   450\t       above.\n   451\t     - An occurrence inside a lambda body is discharged only by an\n   452\t       unconditional definition of that name that is **proven to\n   453\t       execute before every application of the enclosing closure**.\n   454\t       The body runs at application time, and the applications the\n   455\t       image performs are exactly its application sites\n   456\t       (`:applications-fn`, section 4.1). No value-flow analysis\n   457\t       bounds which closures a site can apply, so every site is\n   458\t       treated as a possible application of every closure the image\n   459\t       creates: a definition discharges a body occurrence only when\n   460\t       it dominates every application site in the main sequence,\n   461\t       under the same order rules as a main-sequence occurrence. A\n   462\t       site inside another body needs no separate case: it executes\n   463\t       only after some main-sequence site has executed, which the\n   464\t       definition dominates, or after halt, by which an unconditional\n   465\t       definition has executed. An image with no application site\n   466\t       discharges a body occurrence against every unconditional\n   467\t       definition of the name: nothing applies the closure before\n   468\t       halt, and after halt the read runs against the module store\n   469\t       the relocation carries (section 7.3), never the receiver's\n   470\t       ambient bindings. Where any site is not dominated, the\n   471\t       obligation is **retained** and must be declared by the\n   472\t       manifest exactly as a conditional definition's must. Revision\n   473\t       r5 discharged a body occurrence against any later\n   474\t       unconditional definition and left an early application to\n   475\t       \"fail in the child at run time\"; the second half was wrong:\n   476\t       the read does not reliably error, because `resolve-var`\n   527\t\n   528\tEvery refusal is `{:status :refused :reason r}` merged with the step's own\n   529\tevidence, exactly as `yin.vm.linker/refused` builds it.\n   530\t\n   531\t| Reason                  | Step   | Meaning                                  |\n   532\t|-------------------------|--------|------------------------------------------|\n   533\t| `:invalid-request`      | 0      | a request outside the closed key set of  |\n   534\t|                         |        | section 6.3, or with a non-portable value|\n   535\t| `:absent`               | 1 or 2 | no index entry, or no payload at the     |\n   536\t|                         |        | address (root or any part)               |\n   537\t| `:address-mismatch`     | 2      | payload does not hash to its address     |\n   538\t| `:parts-limit`          | 2      | a composition bound on parts, depth, or  |\n   539\t|                         |        | bytes was exceeded                       |\n   540\t| `:hash-mismatch`        | 3      | root value does not match the identity   |\n   541\t| `:descriptor-defect`    | 2 or 4 | row-local or whole-value validation      |\n   542\t|                         |        | failed                                   |\n   543\t| `:contract-mismatch`    | 0      | the request, or the manifest's entry for |\n   544\t|                         |        | the requested format, names an execution |\n   545\t|                         |        | contract the format record does not      |\n   546\t|                         |        | implement                                |\n   547\t| `:use-before-definition`| 5a     | a main-sequence occurrence precedes      |\n   548\t|                         |        | every definition of its name             |\n   549\t| `:undeclared-free`      | 5a     | a free name has no declaration in the    |\n   550\t|                         |        | manifest that delivered the image        |\n   551\t| `:unresolved-free`      | 5b     | an obligation is not discharged by an    |\n   552\t|                         |        | equal profile or manifest                |\n   553\t| `:shadowed-free`        | 5b     | an obligation's name is bound by the     |\n   554\t|                         |        | receiver's free env or store             |\n   555\t| `:unsupported-format`   | 0      | the receiver holds no kernel or format   |\n   556\t|                         |        | record for the requested format          |\n  1870\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1871\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1872\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1873\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1874\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1875\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1876\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1877\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1878\t`:blake3`.\n  1879\t\n  1880\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1881\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n  1882\tpurely local composition, over `dao.stream.rpc` on a ring-buffer pair\n  1883\tserved by `dao.jing.remote/serve-content!`'s handlers). Reimplement\n  1884\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1885\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  1886\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  1887\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  1888\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  1889\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1890\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1891\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1892\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1893\t\n  1894\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1895\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (a signed assertion\n  1896\tby a declared principal resolves; a bare `:asserted-by` with no proof is\n  1897\t`:unauthenticated`; a bad signature is `:unauthenticated`; an attested\n  1898\tlog's assertion copied onto another stream is `:unauthenticated`; an\n  1899\tundeclared principal is ignored; a signed retraction bound to an\n  1900\tassertion's id removes that assertion only, and a retraction naming no\n  1901\tassertion or signed by another principal is discarded; an exact\n  1902\tduplicate envelope is honored once and never counted as equivocation;\n  1903\ta replayed sequence and a distinct equivocating pair are discarded; two\n  1904\tproven assertions refuse `:ambiguous-name`; snapshot advance). Then:\n  1905\tthe manifest and derivation\n  1906\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1907\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1908\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1909\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1910\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n   160\t    (map? batch) (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode batch)\n   161\t    :else (datoms->rows batch)))\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t;; =============================================================================\n   165\t;; The macro expander's input batch (yin.vm.macro.md §2.1, §10.2)\n   166\t;; =============================================================================\n   167\t\n   168\t(defn- definition-name\n   169\t  \"The name of a `(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)` AST node (§2.2), else nil.\"\n   170\t  [{:keys [type operator operands]}]\n   171\t  (when (and (= :application type)\n   172\t             (= :variable (:type operator))\n   173\t             (= 'yin/def (:name operator))\n   174\t             (= 2 (count operands))\n   175\t             (= :literal (:type (first operands)))\n   176\t             (symbol? (:value (first operands))))\n   177\t    (:value (first operands))))\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\t(defn- ast-children\n   181\t  \"`[[path-suffix child] ...]` of one AST node in grammar order. A suffix\n   226\t        :else (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported program batch member\"\n   227\t                              {:rule :batch-member, :member member}))))\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn program-batch\n   231\t  \"Encode frontend output as the expander's input batch (§2.1):\n   232\t   `[:yin.program/batch trees run-index declaration-rows harvest-rows]`.\n   233\t   Each member — a map AST or a `:yin/*` datom batch — projects to one tree\n   234\t   packet; `run-index` selects the one that becomes the program. Harvest\n   235\t   rows name every `(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)` occurrence in source\n   236\t   declaration order, member by member; declaration rows name those whose\n   237\t   lambda the frontend flagged `:macro?`. No syntax object crosses: every\n   238\t   code field is canonical rows.\"\n   239\t  ([member] (program-batch [member] 0))\n   240\t  ([members run-index]\n   241\t   (let [asts (mapv member-ast members)\n   242\t         trees (mapv (fn [ast]\n   243\t                       (let [{:keys [root rows]} (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)]\n   244\t                         [root (vec (vals rows))]))\n   675\t     'yin/application (fn [operator operands]\n   676\t                        (need-packet 'yin/application operator)\n   677\t                        (doseq [o operands] (need-packet 'yin/application o))\n   678\t                        (application-packet operator (vec operands))),\n   679\t     'yin/if (fn [t c a]\n   680\t               (doseq [x [t c a]] (need-packet 'yin/if x))\n   681\t               (construct [:if (first t) (first c) (first a)] [t c a])),\n   682\t     'yin/sequence-body sequence-body,\n   683\t     'yin/make-lambda (fn [params-tree body]\n   684\t                        (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda params-tree))]\n   685\t                          (when-not (and (= :literal (row-tag row))\n   686\t                                         (vector? (nth row 2))\n   687\t                                         (every? symbol? (nth row 2)))\n   688\t                            (throw-prelude \"yin/make-lambda reads a literal parameter vector\"\n   689\t                                           {:op 'yin/make-lambda}))\n   690\t                          (lambda-packet (nth row 2) (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda body)))),\n   691\t     'yin/make-def (fn [name-tree value-tree]\n   692\t                     (application-packet (construct [:variable 'yin/def] [])\n   693\t                                         [(literal-packet (name-of name-tree))\n   694\t                                          (need-packet 'yin/make-def value-tree)])),\n   695\t     'yin/name-of name-of,\n   696\t     'yin/gensym-sym gensym}))\n   697\t\n   698\t\n   699\t(def ^:private suspending-tags\n   700\t  #{:vm/park :vm/resume :dao.stream.apply/call})\n  1248\t                 :body (app {:type :lambda,\n  1249\t                             :params '[l],\n  1250\t                             :body (app (v 'yin/make-def) (v 'fn-name) (v 'l))}\n  1251\t                            (app (v 'yin/make-lambda) (v 'fn-params) (v 'b)))}\n  1252\t                (app (v 'yin/sequence-body) (v 'body)))}))\n  1253\t\n  1254\t\n  1255\t(def stdlib-forms\n  1256\t  \"The standard forms as a row-native batch: one tree defining `defn`,\n  1257\t   declared and harvested. Seed a store by expanding it (`seed-store`).\"\n  1258\t  (let [def-ast {:type :application,\n  1259\t                 :operator {:type :variable, :name 'yin/def},\n  1260\t                 :operands [{:type :literal, :value 'defn} defn-lambda-ast]}]\n  1261\t    [:yin.program/batch\n  1262\t     [(ast->packet def-ast)]\n  1263\t     0\n  1264\t     [[:yin.macro/definition 0 []]]\n  1265\t     [[:yin.macro/harvest 0 0 []]]]))\n  1266\t\n   155\t  [v]\n   156\t  (try (vector-layout v)\n   157\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- in-body-pc?\n   161\t  \"Whether pc `p` lies in one of the closure body spans `spans`.\"\n   162\t  [spans p]\n   163\t  (boolean (some (fn [[_ b r]] (<= b p r)) spans)))\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\t(defn- conditional-ranges\n   167\t  \"The pcs a conditional target range covers in canonical vector `v`\n   168\t   (section 4.1): for every `:jump` or `:branch-false` at pc b with\n   169\t   target t, the pcs strictly between b and t, either direction -- the\n   170\t   fall-through a taken branch skips, and a backward jump's body.\"\n   171\t  [v]\n   172\t  (into #{}\n   173\t        (mapcat (fn [[b t]]\n   174\t                  (when (and (integer? t) (not= b t))\n   175\t                    (range (inc (min b t)) (max b t)))))\n   176\t        (keep (fn [pc]\n   177\t                (let [t (nth v pc)]\n   178\t                  (when (and (vector? t)\n   179\t                             (contains? #{:jump :branch-false}\n   180\t                                        (nth t 0)))\n   181\t                    [pc (nth t 1)])))\n   182\t              (range (count v)))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn- degraded-occurrences\n   186\t  \"The conservative degradation's own occurrence records (section 4.1):\n   187\t   every name retained at no position, inside a body -- a scanner that\n   188\t   cannot read positions retains every occurrence and discharges\n   189\t   nothing.\"\n   190\t  [names]\n   191\t  (vec (sort-by (comp str :name)\n   192\t                (map (fn [n] {:name n, :at nil, :in-body? true}) names))))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(defn- degraded-definitions\n   196\t  \"The conservative degradation's own definition records (section 4.1):\n   197\t   every key retained at no position, conditional -- a definition whose\n   198\t   position is unknown discharges nothing.\"\n   199\t  [names]\n   200\t  (vec (sort-by (comp str :name)\n   201\t                (map (fn [n] {:name n, :at nil, :conditional? true})\n   202\t                     names))))\n   203\t\n   204\t\n   205\t(defn semantic-free-occurrences\n   206\t  \"Every free `:var` occurrence of canonical vector `v` as a section 4.1\n   207\t   record `{:name sym :at pc :in-body? b}`, in pc order (UCF section\n   208\t   7.3.2): a `:var` at pc `p` is bound iff `p` lies in the body of a\n   209\t   `:closure` whose params hold the name, transitively through the body\n   210\t   holding that closure's own pc. Over a vector whose body spans are not\n   211\t   closed, off pc 0, and pairwise disjoint -- anything but the\n   212\t   ast-to-bytecode layout -- every `:var` name degrades to a record with\n   213\t   no position: over-approximating obligations is always admissible.\"\n   214\t  [v]\n   215\t  (try\n   475\t      (vec (keep (fn [t] (when (call? t) {:at nil})) v)))))\n   476\t\n   477\t\n   478\t(defn- register-body-at\n   479\t  \"The index of the declared body of register image map `image` whose pc\n   480\t   range covers `p`, or nil: body 0 is the main program, every other\n   481\t   body a lambda's.\"\n   482\t  [image p]\n   483\t  (some (fn [i]\n   484\t          (let [b (nth (:bodies image) i)]\n   485\t            (when (and (integer? (:start b)) (integer? (:end b))\n   486\t                       (<= (:start b) p (:end b)))\n   487\t              i)))\n   488\t        (range (count (:bodies image)))))\n   489\t\n   490\t\n   491\t(defn- register-in-body?\n   492\t  \"Whether pc `p` of register image map `image` lies in a lambda body\n   493\t   rather than the main program (section 4.1).\"\n   494\t  [image p]\n   495\t  (let [i (register-body-at image p)]\n   496\t    (boolean (and i (pos? i)))))\n   497\t\n   498\t\n   499\t(defn- register-conditional-ranges\n   500\t  \"The conditional target range pcs of a register image's instructions\n   501\t   (section 4.1): a `:jump`'s target is its first operand, a\n   502\t   `:branch-false`'s its second.\"\n   503\t  [image]\n   504\t  (into #{}\n   505\t        (mapcat (fn [[b t]]\n   506\t                  (when (and (integer? t) (not= b t))\n   507\t                    (range (inc (min b t)) (max b t)))))\n   508\t        (keep-indexed\n   509\t          (fn [pc t]\n   510\t            (when (vector? t)\n   511\t              (case (nth t 0)\n   512\t                :jump [pc (nth t 1)]\n   513\t                :branch-false [pc (nth t 2)]\n   514\t                nil)))\n   515\t          (:instructions image))))\n   516\t\n   517\t\n   518\t(defn- register-free-occurrences\n   519\t  \"Every `:load-free` occurrence across all bodies of a register image\n   520\t   map as a section 4.1 record `{:name sym :at pc :in-body? b}`, in pc\n   521\t   order. A register `:load-free` is `[:load-free rd name]`.\"\n   522\t  [image]\n   523\t  (vec (keep-indexed\n   524\t         (fn [pc t]\n   525\t           (when (and (vector? t) (= :load-free (nth t 0)))\n   526\t             {:name (nth t 2), :at pc,\n   527\t              :in-body? (register-in-body? image pc)}))\n   528\t         (:instructions image))))\n   529\t\n   530\t\n   531\t(defn- register-definition-occurrences\n   532\t  \"Every `:store-put` key the register image binds, as a section 4.1\n   533\t   record `{:name key :at pc :conditional? b}`: conditional when a jump\n   534\t   target range or a lambda body encloses the pc (section 4.1). A\n   535\t   register `:store-put` is `[:store-put rd key value]`.\"\n   536\t  [image]\n   537\t  (let [ranges (register-conditional-ranges image)]\n   538\t    (vec (keep-indexed\n   539\t           (fn [pc t]\n   540\t             (when (and (vector? t) (= :store-put (nth t 0)))\n   541\t               {:name (nth t 2), :at pc,\n   542\t                :conditional? (or (contains? ranges pc)\n   543\t                                  (register-in-body? image pc))}))\n   544\t           (:instructions image)))))\n   545\t\n   546\t\n   547\t(defn- register-application-sites\n   548\t  \"Every application site of the register image as a section 4.1 record\n   549\t   `{:at pc}`: a `:call` or `:ffi-call` pc (section 4.1).\"\n   550\t  [image]\n   551\t  (vec (keep-indexed\n   552\t         (fn [pc t]\n   553\t           (when (and (vector? t)\n   554\t                      (contains? #{:call :ffi-call} (nth t 0)))\n   555\t             {:at pc}))\n   556\t         (:instructions image))))\n   557\t\n   558\t\n   559\t;; =============================================================================\n   560\t;; Row-local validation and the parts worklist (sections 5.1, 4.2 step 2)\n  1059\t(defn fetch\n  1060\t  \"Fetches and verifies an image by its identity using handle, index, and\n  1061\t   format record; one surface for all four formats. Returns the verified\n  1062\t   image `{:status :ok ...}` or a qualified refusal.\n  1063\t\n  1064\t   `handle` is any DaoJing content handle; `index` is a map or function\n  1065\t   from identity to Jing address -- the identity function itself for the\n  1066\t   two storage-derived formats, whose identity is its own address\n  1067\t   (section 3); `format` is a format record; `identity` is H or R, a\n  1068\t   root row id, or a vector address. `receiver` is the receiving VM's\n  1069\t   free-name environment `{:free-env :store :primitives :modules}`; the\n  1070\t   4-arity form uses the empty receiver, so only a closed image (no\n  1071\t   retained obligations) is accepted. `opts` carries the admission\n  1072\t   contract `:contract` and the step-2 bounds `:max-parts`, `:max-depth`,\n  1073\t   `:max-bytes`; a bound the caller leaves nil takes `default-bounds`,\n  1074\t   so every fetch path is finite.\n  1075\t\n  1076\t   The steps run in strict order (section 4.2), with no format-specific\n  1077\t   branching:\n  1078\t     0. the requested contract equals the record's   :contract-mismatch\n  1079\t     1. address <- (index identity)                  :absent\n  1080\t     2. the bounded worklist of :parts-fn, each      :absent,\n  1081\t        part read, verified, sized, then row-checked :address-mismatch,\n  1082\t        before any child it names is decoded or      :descriptor-defect,\n  1083\t        enqueued                                     :parts-limit\n  1084\t     3. ((:identity-matches-fn format) identity root :hash-mismatch\n  1085\t     4. ((:validate-fn format) whole) is nil         :descriptor-defect\n  1086\t     5a. the scanners' occurrences join their        :use-before-definition\n  1087\t         definitions: an unconditional definition\n  1088\t         that dominates the occurrence discharges\n  1089\t         it; the rest are retained\n  1090\t     5b. every retained obligation binds in the      :unresolved-free,\n  1091\t         receiver                                    :shadowed-free\n  1092\t     6. the verified image\n  1093\t\n  1094\t   For a multi-part format the whole of steps 4 to 6 is the tree\n  1095\t   assembled by prepending each fetched part's address, the shape\n  1096\t   `validate-rows` takes (section 5.1), and the outcome carries\n  1097\t   `:parts {address body}`.\"\n  1098\t  ([handle index format identity]\n  1099\t   (fetch handle index format identity {}))\n  1100\t  ([handle index format identity receiver]\n  1101\t   (fetch handle index format identity receiver nil))\n  1102\t  ([handle index format identity receiver opts]\n  1103\t   (let [{:keys [contract]} opts]\n  1104\t     (if (and (some? contract) (not= contract (:contract format)))\n  1105\t       (refused :contract-mismatch\n  1106\t                {:expected contract, :actual (:contract format)})\n  1107\t       (if-let [address (index identity)]\n  1108\t         (if-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n  1109\t           (refused :absent {:address address})\n  1110\t           (let [worklist (fetch-parts handle format identity address\n  1111\t                                       opts)]\n  1112\t             (if (refused? worklist)\n  1113\t               worklist\n  1114\t               (let [{:keys [parts multi?]} worklist\n  1115\t                     root-value (get parts address)\n  1116\t                     whole (if multi?\n  1117\t                             {:root identity,\n  1118\t                              :rows (into {}\n  1119\t                                          (map (fn [[a v]] [a (into [a] v)]))\n  1120\t                                          parts)}\n  1121\t                             root-value)]\n  1122\t                 (if-not (matches-identity? format identity root-value)\n  1123\t                   (refused :hash-mismatch\n  1124\t                            {:expected identity,\n  1125\t                             :actual (identity-of format root-value)})\n  1126\t                   (if-let [defect (validation-defect format whole)]\n  1127\t                     (refused :descriptor-defect\n  1128\t                              {:identity identity, :defect defect})\n  1129\t                     (let [joined (undischarged\n  1130\t                                    ((:obligations-fn format) whole)\n  1131\t                                    (scanned format :definitions-fn\n  1132\t                                             whole)\n  1133\t                                    (scanned format :applications-fn\n  1134\t                                             whole))]\n  1135\t                       (or (:defect joined)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
