losures, streams, cursors, parked records), the store-key\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1798:  plain definitions stay executable `yin/def` nodes and are forwarded\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1813:  replaced by stand-ins; their occurrences remain ordinary `yin/def`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1816:  group must name a `(yin/def <literal sym> _)` node; every such node in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1831:  `(yin/def <literal sym> <lambda>)`, i.e., its reconstructed semantic map must have an `:operator` that is a `:variable` node naming `yin/def` (free at that site, per §4.5), its first operand a `:literal` symbol node, and its second operand a `:lambda` node. A\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1838:  a flagged lambda anywhere but the value operand of a `yin/def` as\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1846:- **Missing fact.** A `(yin/def sym v)` with no declaration at its\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1939:|                                                  | true` lambda that is not the value operand of a `yin/def` as `:stray-macro-lambda`, then turn each admitted one into|\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:2016:2. **The store-key domain is the `data` domain** (§2.2): every validator,\n   170\t           (pure '/ checked-divide [1 2 :variadic])\n   171\t           (pure '= = [0 1 2 :variadic])\n   172\t           (pure '== = [0 1 2 :variadic])\n   173\t           (pure '!= not= [1 2 :variadic])\n   174\t           (pure '< < [1 2 :variadic])\n   175\t           (pure '> > [1 2 :variadic])\n   176\t           (pure '<= <= [1 2 :variadic])\n   177\t           (pure '>= >= [1 2 :variadic])\n   178\t           (pure 'not not [1])\n   179\t           (pure 'nil? nil? [1])\n   180\t           (pure 'empty? empty? [1])\n   181\t           (pure 'first first [1])\n   182\t           (pure 'rest (fn [a] (vec (rest a))) [1])\n   183\t           (pure 'conj conj [1 2 :variadic])\n   184\t           (pure 'assoc assoc [3 :variadic])\n   185\t           (pure 'get get [2 3])\n   186\t           (pure 'vec vec [1])\n   187\t           (pure 'bytes->str\n   188\t                 #?(:clj (fn\n   189\t                           ([b] (String. ^bytes b \"UTF-8\"))\n   190\t                           ([b enc] (String. ^bytes b ^String enc)))\n   191\t                    :cljs (fn [b] (.apply js/String.fromCharCode nil b))\n   192\t                    :cljd (fn [b] (dart:core/String.fromCharCodes b)))\n   193\t                 [1 2])\n   194\t           ['yin/def (primitive-entry\n   195\t                       'yin/def\n   196\t                       (fn [k v] {:effect :vm/store-put, :key k, :val v})\n   197\t                       :effectful [2] #{:vm/store-put})]\n   198\t           ['require (primitive-entry\n   199\t                       'require\n   200\t                       (fn [spec]\n   201\t                         (let [ns-sym (if (vector? spec) (first spec) spec)]\n   202\t                           {:effect :module/require, :module ns-sym}))\n   203\t                       :effectful [1] #{:module/require})]])))\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t(def ^:private primitive-profile-keys\n   207\t  [:yin.k/profile :yin.k/class :yin.k/arities :yin.k/effects\n   208\t   :yin.k/host-state])\n   209\t\n   210\t\n   211\t(def primitive-profiles\n   212\t  \"Portable projection of the standard registry, retained as a convenience.\"\n   213\t  (into {} (map (fn [[name entry]]\n   214\t                  [name (select-keys entry primitive-profile-keys)]))\n   215\t        primitives))\n   720\t(defn plain-data?\n   721\t  \"True when `x` is data a row or code datom may carry (§2.2, §2.5): scalars\n   722\t   and collections of them, never a host function or object. Metadata\n   723\t   travels with the value, so it must be plain data too.\"\n   724\t  [x]\n   725\t  (or (nil? x)\n   726\t      (and (cond (or (boolean? x) (number? x) (string? x) (keyword? x)\n   727\t                     (symbol? x))\n   728\t                 true\n   729\t                 (map? x) (and (every? plain-data? (keys x))\n   730\t                               (every? plain-data? (vals x)))\n   731\t                 (coll? x) (every? plain-data? x)\n   732\t                 :else false)\n   733\t           (plain-data? (meta x)))))\n   734\t\n   735\t\n   736\t(defn occurrence-origin?\n   737\t  \"True when `origin` has one of §2.5's portable ruled shapes. `nil` is not\n   738\t   an occurrence; it is accepted separately by the legacy bare-row lane.\n   739\t\n   740\t   A source origin is `[:source medium batch-token member-index]`. Medium and\n   741\t   token are opaque non-nil plain data supplied by the admitting composition,\n   742\t   and the member index is a non-negative integer. An expansion origin names\n   743\t   the portable content address of its expansion record.\"\n   744\t  [origin]\n   745\t  (and (vector? origin)\n   746\t       (case (first origin)\n   747\t         :source (and (= 4 (count origin))\n   748\t                      (some? (nth origin 1))\n   749\t                      (plain-data? (nth origin 1))\n   750\t                      (some? (nth origin 2))\n   751\t                      (plain-data? (nth origin 2))\n   752\t                      (integer? (nth origin 3))\n   753\t                      (not (neg? (nth origin 3))))\n   754\t         :expansion (and (= 2 (count origin))\n   755\t                         (jing/segment-address? (nth origin 1)))\n   756\t         false)))\n   757\t\n   758\t\n   759\t(defn source-origin\n   760\t  \"Construct and validate the source occurrence coordinate owned by a batch\n   761\t   envelope. Throws with `:rule :origin` instead of allowing an incomplete\n   762\t   coordinate to enter a provenance or frontend side table.\"\n   763\t  [medium batch-token member-index]\n   764\t  (let [origin [:source medium batch-token member-index]]\n   765\t    (when-not (occurrence-origin? origin)\n   766\t      (throw (ex-info \"Malformed source occurrence origin\"\n   767\t                      {:rule :origin, :origin origin})))\n   768\t    origin))\n   769\t\n   770\t\n   771\t(defn loaded-code-floor\n   772\t  \"The lowest entity id claimed by the segments in a `{segment-id image}`\n   773\t   code map — each segment id minus its length — or 0 when none is loaded.\n   774\t   A loader minting a fresh local segment id allocates below this floor\n   775\t   (`linearize/ast-loader` for lowered AST batches, `semantic/load-vector`\n   776\t   for canonical instruction vectors), so successive loads never collide\n   777\t   with a live id.\"\n   778\t  [code]\n   779\t  (if (map? code)\n   780\t    (reduce-kv (fn [floor seg image]\n   781\t                 (if (and (integer? seg) (map? image))\n   782\t                   (min floor (- seg (or (:length image) 0)))\n   783\t                   floor))\n   784\t               0\n   785\t               code)\n   786\t    0))\n   787\t\n   788\t\n   789\t;; =============================================================================\n   790\t;; Semantic bytecode: flat content-addressed rows\n   791\t;; =============================================================================\n   792\t;; docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2. One row `[id tag & slots]` per\n   793\t;; distinct node; `id` is `(jing/segment-key [tag & slots])`.\n   794\t\n   795\t(def semantic-bytecode-grammar\n   796\t  \"The §2.3 tag table: tag -> ordered `[field kind]` slots. Position `i` of a\n   797\t   row body (after the tag) holds the map field named at `i`, so this one\n   798\t   table drives both projection and reconstruction.\"\n   799\t  {:literal [[:value :data]],\n   800\t   :variable [[:name :sym]],\n  1230\t\n  1231\t;; parked ids named by resume\n  1232\t[:find ?pid :in $ast :where [$ast _ :vm/resume ?pid _]]\n  1233\t\n  1234\t;; syntax that raises an effect: the tag, to be normalized by the footprint table below\n  1235\t[:find ?tag :in $ast\n  1236\t :where [$ast _ ?tag & _]\n  1237\t        [(contains? #{:stream/make :stream/put :stream/cursor :stream/next\n  1238\t                      :stream/close :dao.stream.apply/call} ?tag)]]\n  1239\t```\n  1240\t\n  1241\tExtraction over segments (`$code` is the union of segment-qualified rows):\n  1242\t\n  1243\t```clojure\n  1244\t;; likewise over segment-qualified rows: derive free names from the\n  1245\t;; instruction vector's own scoping, no separate opcode needed. Unlike\n  1246\t;; AST rows, instructions are positionally addressed within one segment\n  1247\t;; (segment-address, pc), not content-shared sub-vector by sub-vector, so\n  1248\t;; the mixed-occurrence risk §4.5 documents for AST rows may not apply\n  1249\t;; here the same way — this is unverified. `linearize.cljc/lower` exists\n  1250\t;; today (`:162`) but takes `[e a v t m]` datoms, not the row sets this\n  1251\t;; design specifies (§9.1: lower must be adapted to read the row relation\n  1252\t;; instead); no test exercises this query against the row-set-based\n  1253\t;; lowering, so confirm this reasoning when that adaptation lands rather\n  1254\t;; than assuming it.\n  1255\t[:find ?name :in $code % :where [$code _ _ :var ?name] (not (bound? ?name))]\n  1256\t[:find ?key  :in $code :where (or [$code _ _ :store-get ?key]\n  1257\t                                  [$code _ _ :store-put ?key _])]\n  1258\t[:find ?op   :in $code :where [$code _ _ :ffi-call ?op _]]\n  1259\t[:find ?pid  :in $code :where [$code _ _ :resume ?pid]]\n  1260\t[:find ?mn   :in $code\n    70\t  (app (lam '[x] (tail (v 'x))) (lit 42)))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(def ^:private other-program\n    74\t  \"`(* 6 7)`: a different image, for swapped index entries and pairings.\"\n    75\t  (app (v '*) (lit 6) (lit 7)))\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(def ^:private unknown-free\n    79\t  \"`(nope 1)`: a free name no receiver resolves.\"\n    80\t  (app (v 'nope) (lit 1)))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(def ^:private nested-capture\n    84\t  \"`((fn [x] (fn [y] x)) 1)`: `x` read inside the inner body is bound by\n    85\t   the outer closure's params, across the out-of-line bodies.\"\n    86\t  (app (lam '[x] (tail (lam '[y] (v 'x)))) (lit 1)))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- store-put\n    90\t  [k val]\n    91\t  {:type :vm/store-put, :key k, :val val})\n    92\t\n    93\t\n    94\t(def ^:private def-then-use\n    95\t  \"`((fn [_ _] 0) (vm/store-put x 1) x)`: the binding is the first\n    96\t   operand; the second operand reads it after the binding executes.\"\n    97\t  (app (lam '[a b] (lit 0)) (store-put 'x 1) (v 'x)))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(def ^:private use-then-def\n   101\t  \"`((fn [_ _] 0) x (vm/store-put x 1))`: the read precedes every\n   102\t   definition of its name.\"\n   103\t  (app (lam '[a b] (lit 0)) (v 'x) (store-put 'x 1)))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(def ^:private branch-def\n   107\t  \"`((fn [_ _] 0) (if true (vm/store-put x 1) 0) x)`: the binding sits\n   108\t   in an `:if` branch; the read keeps its obligation.\"\n   109\t  (app (lam '[a b] (lit 0))\n   110\t       {:type :if, :test (lit true),\n   111\t        :consequent (store-put 'x 1), :alternate (lit 0)}\n   112\t       (v 'x)))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(def ^:private body-def\n   116\t  \"`((fn [_ _] 0) (fn [] (vm/store-put x 1)) x)`: the binding sits\n   117\t   inside a lambda body.\"\n   118\t  (app (lam '[a b] (lit 0)) (lam '[] (store-put 'x 1)) (v 'x)))\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\t(def ^:private define-then-apply\n   122\t  \"`((fn [_ _] 0) (vm/store-put x 1) ((fn [] x)))`: the binding executes\n   123\t   before the application site that may apply the closure reading x.\"\n   124\t  (app (lam '[a b] (lit 0)) (store-put 'x 1) (app (lam '[] (v 'x)))))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(def ^:private apply-then-define\n   128\t  \"`((fn [_ _] 0) ((fn [] x)) (vm/store-put x 1))`: the closure reading\n   129\t   x is applied before the binding executes.\"\n   130\t  (app (lam '[a b] (lit 0)) (app (lam '[] (v 'x))) (store-put 'x 1)))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(def ^:private scan-vector\n   134\t  \"A hand-built canonical vector: an unconditional binding, one inside a\n   135\t   jump's target range, a call site, and a closure body reading `w`.\"\n   395\t         (linker/address-attribute linker/register-format))))\n   396\t\n   397\t\n   398\t;; =============================================================================\n   399\t;; Section 4.1: the position-bearing scanners\n   400\t;; =============================================================================\n   401\t\n   402\t(deftest ast-scanners-yield-position-bearing-records\n   403\t  (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode def-then-use)\n   404\t        root (:root tree)\n   405\t        {:keys [obligations-fn definitions-fn applications-fn]}\n   406\t        linker/ast-format]\n   407\t    (is (= [{:name 'x, :at [root [[3 0]]], :conditional? false}]\n   408\t           (definitions-fn tree))\n   409\t        \"the store-key query carries the binding row's path\")\n   410\t    (is (= [{:name 'x, :at [root [[3 1]]], :in-body? false}]\n   411\t           (obligations-fn tree))\n   412\t        \"vm/free-names' rules, wrapped to carry each occurrence's path\")\n   413\t    (is (= [{:at [root []]}] (applications-fn tree))\n   414\t        \"one application site per application row\")))\n   415\t\n   416\t\n   417\t(deftest ast-definitions-mark-branch-and-body-bindings-conditional\n   418\t  (let [{:keys [definitions-fn]} linker/ast-format]\n   419\t    (doseq [[label ast] [[:branch branch-def] [:body body-def]]\n   420\t            :let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n   421\t                  root (:root tree)]]\n   422\t      (testing label\n   423\t        (is (= [{:name 'x, :at [root [[3 0] 3]], :conditional? true}]\n   424\t               (definitions-fn tree))\n   425\t            \"any :if branch or lambda body enclosing the binding makes\n   426\t             it conditional\")))))\n   427\t\n   428\t\n   429\t(deftest vector-scanners-yield-position-bearing-records\n   430\t  (doseq [[label format v] [[:SEM linker/semantic-format scan-vector]\n   431\t                            [:H linker/stack-format scan-stack-vector]]]\n   432\t    (testing label\n   433\t      (is (= [{:name 'w, :at 6, :in-body? true}]\n   434\t             ((:obligations-fn format) v))\n   435\t          \"the free occurrence carries its pc and body enclosure\")\n   436\t      (is (= [{:name 'y, :at 0, :conditional? false}\n   437\t              {:name 'z, :at 2, :conditional? true}]\n   438\t             ((:definitions-fn format) v))\n   439\t          \"the binding inside the jump's target range is conditional\")\n   440\t      (is (= [{:at 3}] ((:applications-fn format) v))\n   441\t          \"the call opcode is one application site\"))))\n   442\t\n   443\t\n   444\t(deftest register-scanners-yield-position-bearing-records\n   445\t  (let [image (register-image def-then-use)\n   446\t        {:keys [obligations-fn definitions-fn applications-fn]}\n   447\t        linker/register-format\n   448\t        defs (definitions-fn image)\n   449\t        occs (obligations-fn image)]\n   450\t    (is (= [{:name 'x, :conditional? false}]\n   451\t           (mapv #(select-keys % [:name :conditional?]) defs)))\n   452\t    (is (= [{:name 'x, :in-body? false}]\n   453\t           (mapv #(select-keys % [:name :in-body?]) occs)))\n   454\t    (is (< (:at (first defs)) (:at (first occs)))\n   455\t        \"the definition's pc precedes the occurrence's\")\n   456\t    (is (seq (applications-fn image))\n   457\t        \"the call opcodes are application sites\")))\n   458\t\n   459\t\n   460\t;; =============================================================================\n   915\t               (select-keys res [:bound :address]))\n   916\t            \"the first payload alone exceeds it\")))\n   917\t    (jing/close! store)))\n   918\t\n   919\t\n   920\t(deftest max-bytes-is-checked-before-decode\n   921\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   922\t        ;; one row that is both oversized and malformed: the budget, not\n   923\t        ;; the row, must be what refuses it under a tight bound\n   924\t        big (into [:literal] (concat (range 512) [:extra]))\n   925\t        root (jing/materialize! store big)]\n   926\t    (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :parts-limit, :bound :max-bytes,\n   927\t            :address root}\n   928\t           (select-keys (linker/fetch store {root root} linker/ast-format\n   929\t                                      root receiver {:max-bytes 64})\n   930\t                        [:status :reason :bound :address]))\n   931\t        \"the oversized row is refused before its slots are decoded and\n   932\t         judged\")\n   933\t    (is (= :descriptor-defect\n   934\t           (:reason (linker/fetch store {root root} linker/ast-format\n   935\t                                  root receiver)))\n   936\t        \"under the finite defaults the same row is judged: the refusal\n   937\t         above is the budget's, not the row's\")\n   938\t    (jing/close! store)))\n   939\t\n   940\t\n   941\t(deftest the-parts-budget-is-enforced-at-enqueue-time\n   942\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   943\t        leaf-id (jing/segment-key [:literal 5])\n   944\t        other-leaf (jing/segment-key [:literal 6])\n   945\t        mid-body (app-body leaf-id)\n   946\t        mid-id (jing/segment-key mid-body)\n   947\t        root-body [:application mid-id [other-leaf] false]\n   948\t        root (jing/segment-key root-body)]\n   949\t    (doseq [body [root-body mid-body]]\n   950\t      (jing/materialize! store body))\n   951\t    (let [counts (atom {})\n   952\t          res (linker/fetch (counting-store store counts)\n   953\t                            {root root} linker/ast-format root\n   954\t                            receiver {:max-parts 2})]\n   955\t      (is (= {:bound :max-parts, :address other-leaf}\n   956\t             (select-keys res [:bound :address]))\n   957\t          \"the child beyond the budget is refused while its sibling is\n   958\t           enqueued, before either is fetched\")\n   959\t      (is (zero? (get @counts mid-id 0))\n   960\t          \"no child beyond the budget is ever read\")\n   961\t      (is (= 1 (get @counts root 0))))\n   962\t    (jing/close! store)))\n   963\t\n   964\t\n   965\t(deftest a-fetch-without-explicit-bounds-is-finite\n   966\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   967\t        root (loop [child (jing/segment-key [:literal 1]), i 0]\n   968\t               (if (= i 300)\n   969\t                 child\n   970\t                 (let [body (app-body child)]\n   971\t                   (jing/materialize! store body)\n   972\t                   (recur (jing/segment-key body) (inc i)))))\n   973\t        res (linker/fetch store {root root} linker/ast-format root\n   974\t                          receiver)]\n   975\t    (is (= {:reason :parts-limit, :bound :max-depth}\n   976\t           (select-keys res [:reason :bound]))\n   977\t        \"the linker's own finite `default-bounds` end the walk\")\n   978\t    (jing/close! store)))\n   979\t\n   980\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
