{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '1435,1520p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md | sed -n '1200,1232p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '600,679p;879,920p'\nnl -ba test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc | sed -n '980,1135p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1435\t                :return #{}, :jump #{}, :branch-false #{}, :halt #{}}}})\n  1436\t\n  1437\t\n  1438\t(def ^:private extraction-fns\n  1439\t  \"The `:fns` the §7.7 queries need (§6.3: quoted-symbol keys): the\n  1440\t   effect-raising tag/mnemonic sets are judged by `contains?`.\"\n  1441\t  {'contains? contains?})\n  1442\t\n  1443\t\n  1444\t(defn- extract\n  1445\t  \"One §7.7 extraction query over `db`, its single find column as a set.\"\n  1446\t  [q db]\n  1447\t  (set (map first (query/collect (query/q q db {:fns extraction-fns})))))\n  1448\t\n  1449\t\n  1450\t(def ^:private ast-extraction-queries\n  1451\t  \"§7.7 over `$ast`, the union of the flat rows of the reachable trees,\n  1452\t   verbatim from the design.\"\n  1453\t  {:store-keys '[:find ?key :in $ast\n  1454\t                 :where (or [$ast _ :vm/store-get ?key]\n  1455\t                            [$ast _ :vm/store-put ?key _])],\n  1456\t   :ffi-ops '[:find ?op :in $ast\n  1457\t              :where [$ast _ :dao.stream.apply/call ?op _]],\n  1458\t   :parked-ids '[:find ?pid :in $ast\n  1459\t                 :where [$ast _ :vm/resume ?pid _]],\n  1460\t   ;; syntax that raises an effect: the tag, to be normalized by the\n  1461\t   ;; footprint table\n  1462\t   :effect-raisers '[:find ?tag :in $ast\n  1463\t                     :where [$ast _ ?tag & _]\n  1464\t                     [(contains? #{:stream/make :stream/put :stream/cursor\n  1465\t                                   :stream/next :stream/close\n  1466\t                                   :dao.stream.apply/call}\n  1467\t                                 ?tag)]]})\n  1468\t\n  1469\t\n  1470\t(def ^:private segment-extraction-queries\n  1471\t  \"§7.7 over `$code`, the union of the segment-qualified rows\n  1472\t   (`yin.vm.code/project-segment-qualified`) of the reachable segments,\n  1473\t   verbatim from the design. The segment-side free-name query (derive free\n  1474\t   names from the vector's own scoping) is §7.7's to name but stays\n  1475\t   unverified there; `free-names` over `$ast`/`$occ` is the shipped\n  1476\t   extraction.\"\n  1477\t  {:store-keys '[:find ?key :in $code\n  1478\t                 :where (or [$code _ _ :store-get ?key]\n  1479\t                            [$code _ _ :store-put ?key _])],\n  1480\t   :ffi-ops '[:find ?op :in $code\n  1481\t              :where [$code _ _ :ffi-call ?op _]],\n  1482\t   :parked-ids '[:find ?pid :in $code\n  1483\t                 :where [$code _ _ :resume ?pid]],\n  1484\t   :effect-raisers '[:find ?mn :in $code\n  1485\t                     :where [$code _ _ ?mn & _]\n  1486\t                     [(contains? #{:stream-make :stream-put :stream-cursor\n  1487\t                                   :stream-next :stream-close :ffi-call}\n  1488\t                                 ?mn)]]})\n  1489\t\n  1490\t\n  1491\t(defn- requirements\n  1492\t  \"The §7.7 syntactic requirement set of one relation under contract\n  1493\t   `\\\"v2\\\"`: the three value queries as extracted, and the effect-raising\n  1494\t   tags/mnemonics normalized through the footprint table's `dir` direction\n  1495\t   before any union, so the union is over one vocabulary (§7.7.1).\"\n  1496\t  [db queries dir]\n  1497\t  (let [table (get-in footprint-table [\"v2\" dir])]\n  1498\t    {:store-keys (extract (:store-keys queries) db),\n  1499\t     :ffi-ops (extract (:ffi-ops queries) db),\n  1500\t     :parked-ids (extract (:parked-ids queries) db),\n  1501\t     :effects (into #{} (mapcat table) (extract (:effect-raisers queries) db))}))\n  1502\t\n  1503\t\n  1504\t(defn ast-requirements\n  1505\t  \"§7.7's syntactic requirement set from a tree relation `$ast` — a\n  1506\t   `query/relation` over the flat rows of the reachable trees (e.g.\n  1507\t   `(vals (:rows (ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))`, unioned across trees):\n  1508\t   store keys, FFI ops, parked ids, and effect identifiers, effects\n  1509\t   already normalized by the footprint table. These are the fields of\n  1510\t   `:yin.k/requires` the syntactic queries fill; free names are\n  1511\t   `free-names`, and the value/name/module parts of UCF §7.6.1's fixed\n  1512\t   point remain the walk that consumes this.\"\n  1513\t  [db]\n  1514\t  (requirements db ast-extraction-queries :tags))\n  1515\t\n  1516\t\n  1517\t(defn segment-requirements\n  1518\t  \"The same over a `$code` relation of segment-qualified rows\n  1519\t   (`yin.vm.code/project-segment-qualified`). For every tree,\n  1520\t   `(ast-requirements tree-relation)` and this over its lowered segment's\n  1200\t\n  1201\tExtraction over trees (`$ast` is the union of flat rows of the reachable\n  1202\ttrees):\n  1203\t\n  1204\t```clojure\n  1205\t;; Free-name extraction is a query, not a tag match (§4.5): a :variable\n  1206\t;; occurrence's name is a free-name obligation unless it is bound by an\n  1207\t;; enclosing :lambda on ITS OWN occurrence path. This must be an\n  1208\t;; occurrence-relation query (§2.5's [origin root-address path]), not a\n  1209\t;; row-only one: content-addressed sharing means one :variable row can\n  1210\t;; have several occurrences, and a row-only rule that walks row parent\n  1211\t;; edges instead of per-occurrence paths can find a binder through one\n  1212\t;; occurrence's edge and wrongly call every occurrence of that row bound\n  1213\t;; — undercounting a real dependency, which UCF §7.6.1's conservative\n  1214\t;; fixed point must never do (§4.5). See `test/dao/space/query_test.cljc`'s\n  1215\t;; occurrence-aware rule set for the verified technique (not yet\n  1216\t;; root-scoped as written — §4.5 — a production query must additionally\n  1217\t;; constrain every rule to one root-address, since an unscoped rule set\n  1218\t;; can otherwise resolve a free name in one tree against a binder in a\n  1219\t;; different reachable tree); the shape here is illustrative, not the\n  1220\t;; exact syntax.\n  1221\t[:find ?name :in $ast $occ % ?root\n  1222\t :where [$occ ?root ?path ?v] [?v :variable ?name] (not (bound? ?root ?path ?name))]\n  1223\t\n  1224\t;; store keys read or written by code\n  1225\t[:find ?key :in $ast :where (or [$ast _ :vm/store-get ?key]\n  1226\t                                [$ast _ :vm/store-put ?key _])]\n  1227\t\n  1228\t;; FFI ops\n  1229\t[:find ?op :in $ast :where [$ast _ :dao.stream.apply/call ?op _]]\n  1230\t\n  1231\t;; parked ids named by resume\n  1232\t[:find ?pid :in $ast :where [$ast _ :vm/resume ?pid _]]\n   600\t(def stack-format\n   601\t  \"The `:yin.debruijn.code` format record: stack images identified by H\n   602\t   under the \\\"b1\\\" contract, one canonical vector per image. Free names\n   603\t   are `:load-free` operands, definitions `:store-put` operands,\n   604\t   application sites the call opcodes -- all position-bearing by pc\n   605\t   (section 5.3).\"\n   606\t  {:format              :yin.debruijn.code,\n   607\t   :contract            \"b1\",\n   608\t   :identity-fn         debruijn-code/image-hash,\n   609\t   :identity-matches-fn (fn [H v] (= H (debruijn-code/image-hash v))),\n   610\t   :row-defect-fn       debruijn-code/image-defect,\n   611\t   :validate-fn         debruijn-code/image-defect,\n   612\t   :obligations-fn      stack-free-occurrences,\n   613\t   :definitions-fn      vector-definition-occurrences,\n   614\t   :applications-fn     vector-application-sites,\n   615\t   :parts-fn            (constantly nil)})\n   616\t\n   617\t\n   618\t(def register-format\n   619\t  \"The `:yin.debruijn.register` format record: register images identified\n   620\t   by R under the \\\"r1\\\" contract, one image map per image. Free names\n   621\t   are `[:load-free rd name]` operands across all bodies, definitions\n   622\t   the `:store-put` keys, application sites the call opcodes\n   623\t   (section 5.4).\"\n   624\t  {:format              :yin.debruijn.register,\n   625\t   :contract            \"r1\",\n   626\t   :identity-fn         debruijn-register-code/register-hash,\n   627\t   :identity-matches-fn (fn [R v]\n   628\t                          (= R (debruijn-register-code/register-hash v))),\n   629\t   :row-defect-fn       debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect,\n   630\t   :validate-fn         debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect,\n   631\t   :obligations-fn      register-free-occurrences,\n   632\t   :definitions-fn      register-definition-occurrences,\n   633\t   :applications-fn     register-application-sites,\n   634\t   :parts-fn            (constantly nil)})\n   635\t\n   636\t\n   637\t(def semantic-format\n   638\t  \"The `:yin.semantic/code` format record: the canonical positional\n   639\t   instruction vector stored as the exact payload at its own\n   640\t   `segment-key` (UCF section 7.3.4), under the \\\"v2\\\" contract. Identity\n   641\t   and address are one preimage; step 3 still runs, because it is the\n   642\t   only check that the index did not point the identity at a different,\n   643\t   correctly stored payload (section 4.2). Free names are `:var`\n   644\t   operands, definitions `:store-put` operands, application sites the\n   645\t   call opcodes (section 5.2).\"\n   646\t  {:format              :yin.semantic/code,\n   647\t   :contract            \"v2\",\n   648\t   :identity-fn         jing/segment-key,\n   649\t   :identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?,\n   650\t   :row-defect-fn       code/well-formed-vector?,\n   651\t   :validate-fn         code/well-formed-vector?,\n   652\t   :obligations-fn      semantic-free-occurrences,\n   653\t   :definitions-fn      vector-definition-occurrences,\n   654\t   :applications-fn     vector-application-sites,\n   655\t   :parts-fn            (constantly nil)})\n   656\t\n   657\t\n   658\t(def ast-format\n   659\t  \"The `:yin.ast/code` format record: one row body `[tag & slots]` per\n   660\t   address (D3), the root row's id the tree's identity, under the \\\"v2\\\"\n   661\t   contract. Step 2 is a bounded worklist over the grammar's\n   662\t   `node`/`nodes` slots; the whole tree is assembled for step 4 by\n   663\t   prepending each part's address, the shape `validate-rows` takes. All\n   664\t   three scanners are Datalog over the rows, position-bearing by\n   665\t   occurrence path (section 5.1).\"\n   666\t  {:format              :yin.ast/code,\n   667\t   :contract            \"v2\",\n   668\t   :identity-fn         jing/segment-key,\n   669\t   :identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?,\n   670\t   :row-defect-fn       row-local-defect,\n   671\t   :validate-fn         vm/validate-rows,\n   672\t   :obligations-fn      tree-free-name-occurrences,\n   673\t   :definitions-fn      tree-definition-occurrences,\n   674\t   :applications-fn     tree-application-sites,\n   675\t   :parts-fn            body-child-ids})\n   676\t\n   677\t\n   678\t;; =============================================================================\n   679\t;; The H and R indexes (section 6)\n   879\t  (try (let [get-fn (:get-bytes-fn handle)]\n   880\t         (if (fn? get-fn) (get-fn address missing) missing))\n   881\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   882\t         missing)))\n   883\t\n   884\t\n   885\t(defn- decoded\n   886\t  \"The value of canonical bytes bs, or nil when they do not decode.\"\n   887\t  [bs]\n   888\t  (try (cbor/decode bs)\n   889\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   890\t         nil)))\n   891\t\n   892\t\n   893\t(defn- byte-count\n   894\t  \"The length of host bytes bs, for the `:max-bytes` bound.\"\n   895\t  [bs]\n   896\t  #?(:clj (alength ^bytes bs)\n   897\t     :cljs (.-length bs)\n   898\t     :cljd (.-length ^typed/Uint8List bs)))\n   899\t\n   900\t\n   901\t(defn- identity-of\n   902\t  \"The identity `value` mints under the format, or nil when it cannot be\n   903\t   minted at all (a malformed payload mints no identity). Used by\n   904\t   `publish!` and for refusal evidence, never by verification: step 3 is\n   905\t   `:identity-matches-fn`, directed by the identity the request carries\n   906\t   (I5).\"\n   907\t  [format value]\n   908\t  (try ((:identity-fn format) value)\n   909\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   910\t         nil)))\n   911\t\n   912\t\n   913\t(defn- matches-identity?\n   914\t  \"Step 3's check, directed by the identity the request carries. False\n   915\t   when the payload cannot be matched at all (a malformed payload\n   916\t   matches no identity).\"\n   917\t  [format identity value]\n   918\t  (try ((:identity-matches-fn format) identity value)\n   919\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ false)))\n   920\t\n   980\t\n   981\t;; =============================================================================\n   982\t;; Section 4.2 step 5a: the occurrence/definition join\n   983\t;; =============================================================================\n   984\t\n   985\t(deftest a-definition-discharges-a-use-after-it\n   986\t  (doseq [[label format mint] formats]\n   987\t    (testing label\n   988\t      (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   989\t            {:keys [identity index]} (publish store format\n   990\t                                              (mint def-then-use))\n   991\t            res (linker/fetch store index format identity)]\n   992\t        (is (linker/ok? res))\n   993\t        (is (= [] (:obligations res))\n   994\t            \"the unconditional definition dominating the read discharges\n   995\t             it: the image is closed\")\n   996\t        (jing/close! store)))))\n   997\t\n   998\t\n   999\t(deftest a-use-before-every-definition-is-use-before-definition\n  1000\t  (doseq [[label format mint] formats]\n  1001\t    (testing label\n  1002\t      (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1003\t            image (mint use-then-def)\n  1004\t            {:keys [identity index]} (publish store format image)\n  1005\t            res (linker/fetch store index format identity)]\n  1006\t        (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :use-before-definition,\n  1007\t                :name 'x}\n  1008\t               (select-keys res [:status :reason :name])))\n  1009\t        (is (= (:at (first ((:obligations-fn format) image))) (:at res))\n  1010\t            \"naming the occurrence and its position\")\n  1011\t        (jing/close! store)))))\n  1012\t\n  1013\t\n  1014\t(deftest a-conditional-definition-discharges-nothing\n  1015\t  (doseq [[label format mint] formats]\n  1016\t    (testing label\n  1017\t      (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1018\t            {:keys [identity index]} (publish store format\n  1019\t                                              (mint branch-def))]\n  1020\t        (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :unresolved-free, :name 'x}\n  1021\t               (select-keys (linker/fetch store index format identity)\n  1022\t                            [:status :reason :name]))\n  1023\t            \"an occurrence whose only definitions are conditional and\n  1024\t             earlier retains its obligation\")\n  1025\t        (jing/close! store)))))\n  1026\t\n  1027\t\n  1028\t(deftest a-definition-in-a-lambda-body-discharges-nothing\n  1029\t  (doseq [[label format mint] vector-formats]\n  1030\t    (testing label\n  1031\t      (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1032\t            {:keys [identity index]} (publish store format\n  1033\t                                              (mint body-def))]\n  1034\t        ;; the out-of-line body lands after the main sequence, so the\n  1035\t        ;; only definition is conditional and later\n  1036\t        (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :use-before-definition,\n  1037\t                :name 'x}\n  1038\t               (select-keys (linker/fetch store index format identity)\n  1039\t                            [:status :reason :name])))\n  1040\t        (jing/close! store))))\n  1041\t  (testing \"AST\"\n  1042\t    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1043\t          {:keys [identity index]}\n  1044\t          (publish store linker/ast-format\n  1045\t                   (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode body-def))]\n  1046\t      ;; the tree's slot order puts the operand before the read: the\n  1047\t      ;; only definition is conditional and earlier\n  1048\t      (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :unresolved-free, :name 'x}\n  1049\t             (select-keys (linker/fetch store index linker/ast-format\n  1050\t                                        identity)\n  1051\t                          [:status :reason :name])))\n  1052\t      (jing/close! store))))\n  1053\t\n  1054\t\n  1055\t(deftest a-definition-dominating-every-application-discharges-a-body-occurrence\n  1056\t  (doseq [[label format mint] vector-formats]\n  1057\t    (testing label\n  1058\t      (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1059\t            {:keys [identity index]} (publish store format\n  1060\t                                              (mint define-then-apply))\n  1061\t            res (linker/fetch store index format identity)]\n  1062\t        (is (linker/ok? res))\n  1063\t        (is (= [] (:obligations res))\n  1064\t            \"the binding executes before every application site, so the\n  1065\t             body occurrence is discharged\")\n  1066\t        (jing/close! store)))))\n  1067\t\n  1068\t\n  1069\t(deftest an-application-before-the-definition-retains-the-obligation\n  1070\t  (doseq [[label format mint] formats]\n  1071\t    (testing label\n  1072\t      (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1073\t            {:keys [identity index]} (publish store format\n  1074\t                                              (mint apply-then-define))]\n  1075\t        (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :unresolved-free, :name 'x}\n  1076\t               (select-keys (linker/fetch store index format identity)\n  1077\t                            [:status :reason :name]))\n  1078\t            \"the site the definition does not dominate keeps the\n  1079\t             obligation; for the tree the root application is itself a\n  1080\t             site nothing precedes\")\n  1081\t        (jing/close! store)))))\n  1082\t\n  1083\t\n  1084\t(deftest a-body-occurrence-with-no-application-site-is-discharged\n  1085\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1086\t        address (content/materialize-vector! store no-site-vector)]\n  1087\t    (is (linker/ok? (linker/fetch store {address address}\n  1088\t                                  linker/semantic-format address))\n  1089\t        \"nothing applies the closure before halt, so the body occurrence\n  1090\t         runs against every unconditional definition of its name\")\n  1091\t    (jing/close! store)))\n  1092\t\n  1093\t\n  1094\t(deftest an-unreadable-vector-layout-degrades-conservatively\n  1095\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1096\t        address (content/materialize-vector! store unreadable-vector)\n  1097\t        format linker/semantic-format]\n  1098\t    (is (= [{:name 'q, :at nil, :in-body? true}]\n  1099\t           ((:obligations-fn format) unreadable-vector))\n  1100\t        \"every occurrence is retained, at no position\")\n  1101\t    (is (= [{:name 'x, :at nil, :conditional? true}]\n  1102\t           ((:definitions-fn format) unreadable-vector))\n  1103\t        \"no definition discharges anything\")\n  1104\t    (is (= [{:at nil}] ((:applications-fn format) unreadable-vector))\n  1105\t        \"no application position is usable\")\n  1106\t    (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :unresolved-free, :name 'q}\n  1107\t           (select-keys (linker/fetch store {address address} format\n  1108\t                                      address)\n  1109\t                        [:status :reason :name])))\n  1110\t    (jing/close! store)))\n  1111\t\n  1112\t\n  1113\t(deftest obligations-are-checked-by-name-and-record\n  1114\t  (let [occ {:name '+, :at 0, :in-body? false}]\n  1115\t    (is (nil? (linker/free-name-defect {:primitives {'+ 0}} [occ]))\n  1116\t        \"a legacy symbol-keyed registry discharges the name\")\n  1117\t    (is (nil? (linker/free-name-defect\n  1118\t                {:primitives {{:name 'f, :at 0, :in-body? true} 0}}\n  1119\t                [{:name 'f, :at 1, :in-body? false}]))\n  1120\t        \"a registry keyed by the scanner's own records discharges by\n  1121\t         name: a composition that derives its receiver from the same\n  1122\t         scan binds every name it scanned\")\n  1123\t    (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :unresolved-free, :name 'nope}\n  1124\t           (linker/free-name-defect receiver\n  1125\t                                    [{:name 'nope, :at 0,\n  1126\t                                      :in-body? false}])))\n  1127\t    (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :shadowed-free, :name '+}\n  1128\t           (linker/free-name-defect (assoc receiver :free-env {'+ 0})\n  1129\t                                    [occ])))))\n  1130\t\n  1131\t\n  1132\t;; =============================================================================\n  1133\t;; Identity under every registered algorithm (S11.6 of the master spec)\n  1134\t;; =============================================================================\n  1135\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"Two concrete scanner concerns have emerged: `yin/def` is an ordinary application in encoded ASTs, but the definition scan only matches `:vm/store-put` rows; and the AST application scan records the enclosing row before its operands, although application happens after operand evaluation. I’m checking both against the spec’s dominance rules and existing fixtures."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '1,32p;255,283p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc | sed -n '380,440p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1860,1878p'\ngit status --short\ngit diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '1,32p;255,283p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc | sed -n '380,440p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1860,1878p'\ngit status --short\ngit diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker\n     2\t  \"The code linker (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md): fetches and verifies\n     3\t   code over a DaoJing content handle -- a local store, a\n     4\t   `dao.jing.dht/create-content-dht` handle, or a\n     5\t   `dao.jing.remote/content-client` over DaoStream.\n     6\t\n     7\t   `fetch` is one format-neutral admission-then-six-step function\n     8\t   (sections 4.1-4.2). A format record supplies the contract, the\n     9\t   identity mint and match, the row-local validator, the whole-value\n    10\t   validator, the three position-bearing scanners of section 4.1\n    11\t   (`:obligations-fn`, `:definitions-fn`, `:applications-fn`), and the\n    12\t   parts worklist; the four records are `ast-format`, `semantic-format`,\n    13\t   `stack-format`, and `register-format` (section 5). Storage\n    14\t   addresses (`jing/segment-key`) and VM identities (H, R) are separate\n    15\t   preimages for the de Bruijn formats and the same preimage for the\n    16\t   storage-derived ones, so step 2 checks the address and step 3 checks\n    17\t   the identity; neither subsumes the other (I5).\n    18\t\n    19\t   The handle, the index, the format record, and the receiver environment\n    20\t   are explicit arguments. There is no global loader, registry, callback,\n    21\t   or cache here, and every outcome -- success or refusal -- is a returned\n    22\t   plain data map (section 4.3).\"\n    23\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]])\n    24\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    25\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    26\t            [dao.space.query :as query]\n    27\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    28\t            [yin.vm.code :as code]\n    29\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as debruijn-code]\n    30\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-linearize :as linearize]\n    31\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as debruijn-register-code]\n    32\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile :as register-compile]\n   255\t   6.1): a `:node` slot's step is its row position, a `:nodes` slot's\n   256\t   the pair `[position i]`. A bare position evaluates before the\n   257\t   operands of the `:nodes` slot that follows it.\"\n   258\t  [a b]\n   259\t  (cond\n   260\t    (and (integer? a) (integer? b)) (compare a b)\n   261\t    (integer? a) -1\n   262\t    (integer? b) 1\n   263\t    :else (let [n (min (count a) (count b))]\n   264\t            (loop [i 0]\n   265\t              (if (= i n)\n   266\t                (compare (count a) (count b))\n   267\t                (let [c (compare (nth a i) (nth b i))]\n   268\t                  (if (zero? c) (recur (inc i)) c)))))))\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\t(defn- path-order\n   272\t  \"The execution order of two occurrence paths from one root (section\n   273\t   4.1's tree order): slot order at the first step where they diverge.\"\n   274\t  [a b]\n   275\t  (let [n (min (count a) (count b))]\n   276\t    (loop [i 0]\n   277\t      (if (= i n)\n   278\t        (compare (count a) (count b))\n   279\t        (let [c (step-order (nth a i) (nth b i))]\n   280\t          (if (zero? c) (recur (inc i)) c))))))\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\t(defn- path-before?\n   380\t          (cesk-return state nil env k value))\n   381\t        :lambda (let [{:keys [params body]} node]\n   382\t                  (cesk-return\n   383\t                    state\n   384\t                    nil\n   385\t                    env\n   386\t                    k\n   387\t                    {:type :closure, :params params, :body body, :env env}))\n   388\t        :application (cesk-return\n   389\t                       state\n   390\t                       (:operator node)\n   391\t                       env\n   392\t                       {:frame node, :next k, :env env, :type :eval-operator}\n   393\t                       (:value state))\n   394\t        :if (cesk-return state\n   395\t                         (:test node)\n   396\t                         env\n   397\t                         {:frame node, :next k, :env env, :type :eval-test}\n   398\t                         (:value state))\n   399\t        :dao.stream.apply/call\n   400\t        (let [operands (or (:operands node) [])\n   401\t              op (:op node)]\n   402\t          (if (empty? operands)\n   403\t            (park-and-call state op [] k env)\n   404\t            (cesk-return state\n   405\t                         (first operands)\n   406\t                         env\n   407\t                         {:frame {:op op, :operands operands, :evaluated []},\n   408\t                          :next k,\n   409\t                          :env env,\n   410\t                          :type :dao.stream.apply/eval-operand}\n   411\t                         (:value state))))\n   412\t        :vm/gensym (let [prefix (or (:prefix node) \"id\")\n   413\t                         [id s'] (engine/gensym state prefix)]\n   414\t                     (assoc s'\n   415\t                            :value id\n   416\t                            :control nil\n   417\t                            :halted? (nil? k)))\n   418\t        :vm/store-get (cesk-return state nil env k (get store (:key node)))\n   419\t        :vm/store-put (let [key (:key node)\n   420\t                            value (:val node)\n   421\t                            new-store (assoc store key value)]\n   422\t                        (assoc state\n   423\t                               :store new-store\n   424\t                               :value value\n   425\t                               :control nil\n   426\t                              