hat answered outside the contract is reported with its answer retained,\n   656\t   never folded into a meaning nobody chose. Blocked and ended members\n   657\t   never prevent later members from being checked, and a member that\n   658\t   yielded a payload loses its turn, so a continuously ready member cannot\n   659\t   starve another.\n   660\t\n   661\t   The effect is materialize!, which answers ok or throws: :failed is\n   662\t   unreachable, and a throwing effect propagates before any cursor moves,\n   663\t   so the caller's state is untouched and the same payload is reprocessed\n   664\t   from the same cursor once the backend succeeds.\"\n   665\t  [handle state]\n   666\t  (let [n (count (:members state))]\n   667\t    (if (zero? n)\n   668\t      {:state state, :signal :dao.stream/blocked}\n   669\t      (let [effect (fn [payload]\n   670\t                     {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   671\t                      :address (materialize! handle payload)})]\n   672\t        (loop [i (:next state)\n   673\t               scanned 0\n   674\t               state' state]\n   675\t          (if (>= scanned n)\n   676\t            {:state state'\n   677\t             :signal (if (every? #(= :dao.stream/end (:status %))\n   678\t                                 (:members state'))\n   679\t                       :dao.stream/end\n   680\t                       :dao.stream/blocked)}\n   681\t            (let [member (nth (:members state') i)\n   682\t                  r (observe/step (:stream member) (:cursor member) effect)]\n   683\t              (case (:status r)\n   684\t                :advance\n   685\t                {:state (-> state'\n   686\t                            (assoc-in [:members i :cursor] (:cursor r))\n   687\t                            (assoc-in [:members i :status] :dao.stream/ok)\n   688\t                            (assoc :next (mod (inc i) n)))\n   689\t                 :signal :dao.stream/ok\n   690\t                 :addre